{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["Scripture states here: <b>And He called to Moses, and YHWH spoke to him</b> — and not so in all other places, because Moses was not able to enter the Tent of Meeting, given that he was drawing near to the place where the God was, but only by means of a call with which He would call him, as it was already said to Moses (Exodus 25:22): \"And I will meet with you there and speak with you from above the covering\" (asher iovad lekha shamah), and since he knew that HaShem was enthroned upon the cherubim there, he was afraid to enter the Tent at all until He would call him, as He did at Mount Sinai, of which it says (Exodus 24:16): \"And He called to Moses on the seventh day from within the cloud.\" Or Moses did not know that the Glory was in the Tent and that the divine speech would come to him from there, for the cloud had not covered it until the eighth day according to the opinion of our Sages (Sifra, below ad loc.), and after the call Moses came into the Tent, into the innermost sanctum, as they expounded (Torat Kohanim, after chapter 16:1): \"Aaron — lest he come; and Moses — lest he come.\" But this is not the way of the plain sense in this verse, and I have already explained it above (Exodus 40:34). And our Sages said (Torat Kohanim, chapter 1:7), that to every instance of speaking, every utterance, and every command, a call preceded, meaning that He would say to him: \"Moses, Moses,\" and he would say: \"Here I am,\" and this is an expression of affection and an urging toward Moses. Now according to their opinion, He mentioned this here because it is the beginning of the divine speech that came to him from the Tent of Meeting, to teach concerning all of them, that such would be its rule all the days, in all the Torah, and \"from the Tent of Meeting\" according to their opinion is fronted: \"And He called to him from the Tent of Meeting, and YHWH spoke to him in the Tent,\" for Moses was there. But the syntactic arrangement of the verse according to its plain sense and meaning is: \"And YHWH called to Moses, and He spoke to him from the Tent of Meeting.\" And by way of truth, it is like \"And to Moses He said: Go up to YHWH\" (Exodus 24:1), and its secret is known from the standing at Mount Sinai and in the Ten Commandments, and I have already hinted at it there."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :register {:flags {0 ["God"]}}, :notes {0 "The parenthetical (אשר אועד לך שמה) appears to be an alternative textual reading of the Exodus 25:22 phrase, rendered hyper-literally; I have transliterated it as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:49:30.276076070Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}